<!--
  tinker_full.urdf.xacro
  ======================
  Full Tinker for Isaac Lab nav sim: chassis + xArm + pan-tilt (from
  tracer_mini_manipulator.urdf.xacro) PLUS four wheel articulations
  (two driven front wheels, two passive rear swivel-casters) so PhysX
  can simulate the diff-drive base.

  Frame conventions (tracer_mini-native):
    * base_link is at the xArm mount point on the chassis.
    * +X is the robot's forward direction (chassis long axis).
    * +Y is the robot's left.
    * +Z is up.
    * chassis bottom is at +0.03 in base_link frame, top at +1.577
      (per the chassis mesh extents).

  Wheel layout — X positions anchor the wheel rig under the chassis-
  collision-box center; per-wheel Z-offsets computed so both wheels'
  ground-contacts land at the same level (front and rear radii differ).
  Rear wheels are passive swivel casters (matching real Tracer Mini
  hardware), with the trailing wheel offset −caster_trail along −X of
  the swivel frame. xArm's forward tipping moment is balanced by a
  20 kg `ballast` link (modeling the real Tinker's batteries +
  electronics + computer that aren't in the tracer_mini SolidWorks CAD).

    front_left_wheel_joint  at base_link + ( 0.00, +0.125, -0.025 )
    front_right_wheel_joint at base_link + ( 0.00, -0.125, -0.025 )
    rear_left_swivel_joint  at base_link + (-0.25, +0.125, -0.0475)
    rear_right_swivel_joint at base_link + (-0.25, -0.125, -0.0475)
    rear_*_wheel relative to swivel: (-0.025, 0, 0)  (caster trail)

  Wheel-bottom in base_link frame is at z = -0.0775 (the ground reference);
  spawn base_link at world z ≈ 0.0775 so wheels rest on the ground plane.
-->
